VARISPEED_EMUS harness (tools/varispeed_emus_harness.py): ot_emu logs every arrival at the
DSP voice kernel's entry (payload A P:0x40b on core 0, B P:0x20e on core 1) -- core,
instruction count, x:$418 (track offset), LC (pass), x:$40, y:$40 (the increment), r7,
and the voice record's word +$1E (bit 12: a trig) -- to $OT_VEM_LOG ('%o' = this process's
stdout path + '.vem', so each --scenario child writes its own; '%d' = the pid).
Apply ONLY in a scratch octabam copy (base a67a1112): git apply, then
  cmake -B out/emu -S tools/emu/ot_emu && cmake --build out/emu --target ot_emu
(the ot_emu target alone). Never in a shared clone.

VEM4G (the DSP load guard, IMPL §10) adds, all gated by environment variables: with
--dsp-stopwatch and OT_SW_OUT=FILE, every stopwatch pair's instructions AND datasheet cycles
(dsp56kEmu's calcOpcodeCycles, no memory stalls) are written to FILE ("k instr cycles" per
line); OT_SW_EXTRA="core:start:stop,..." adds stopwatches (k = 1, 2, ...). The guard's DSP
measurements used the four-track loops B P:0x17a..0x333 (core 1) and A P:0x372..0x53e (core 0),
built into a separate directory (out/emu_cyc) so the harness binary stayed as it was.

